{
 "name": "The Mission House",
 "address": "1146 Florida Street, San Francisco, CA",
 "photographer": "Olga Soboleva",
 "description": "Hidden behind an eye-catching Victorian fa\u00e7ade lies 1146 Florida, a three-bedroom, three-and-a-half bath home encompassing nearly 3,000 square feet of living space in the vibrant Mission District. Designed by Tom McElroy Architecture, this uber-upgraded property provides the penultimate in sophisticated living, all within one of San Francisco\u2019s most celebrated neighborhoods.\n\nSpanning three spacious levels, this home underwent an extensive renovation, resulting in a modern gem replete with exquisite finishes. The entertainment possibilities are endless, thanks to an open-concept floor plan and lushly landscaped garden with built-in barbecue, fountain, pergola, and fire pit \u2013 indoor-outdoor living meant to make the most of the best climate in the city. \n\nJust a block away from the booming 24th Street corridor, this home is step\ns away from some of the city\u2019s highlights: eateries, coffee shops, and all the unique offerings that define San Francisco. There\u2019s a reason everyone gathers in the Mission \u2013 and many compelling factors that will draw you to call 1146 Florida home. \n\n*Square footage is approximate, per public records",
